---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");

const title = "Terms of Service";
const description =
    "The terms of use for the Remote Mouse Jiggler Android application: licence, acceptable use, hardware compatibility, intellectual property, warranty and liability.";

const updated = new Date().toLocaleDateString("en-GB", {
    month: "long",
    day: "numeric",
    year: "numeric",
});

const schema = [
    {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "@id": `${SITE.url}terms/#breadcrumb`,
        itemListElement: [
            {
                "@type": "ListItem",
                position: 1,
                name: "Home",
                item: SITE.url,
            },
            {
                "@type": "ListItem",
                position: 2,
                name: "Terms of service",
                item: `${SITE.url}terms/`,
            },
        ],
    },
    {
        "@type": "WebPage",
        "@id": `${SITE.url}terms/#webpage`,
        url: `${SITE.url}terms/`,
        name: `${title} · ${SITE.name}`,
        description,
        isPartOf: { "@id": `${SITE.url}#website` },
        breadcrumb: { "@id": `${SITE.url}terms/#breadcrumb` },
    },
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} titleSuffix={title} schema={schema}>
    <div class="container legal">
        <nav class="legal__crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
            <a href={`${base}/`}>Home</a>
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <span aria-current="page">Terms of service</span>
        </nav>

        <header class="legal__head">
            <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
            <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
            <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
        </header>

        <div class="legal__body prose">
            <p>
                These terms govern your use of the Remote Mouse Jiggler Android
                application (package: <code>{SITE.packageName}</code>), developed
                by <strong>{SITE.developerName}</strong> ({SITE.developer}). By
                installing or using the application you agree to these terms. If
                you do not agree, please do not use the application.
            </p>

            <h2>1. Licence and permitted use</h2>
            <p>
                The application is provided free of charge for personal and
                commercial use. You may use it to control any Bluetooth host you
                own or are authorised to control. The source code is published
                under the MIT licence, and the app name, icon and branding remain
                the property of the developer.
            </p>

            <h2>2. Responsibility and compliance</h2>
            <p>
                You are responsible for how you use the application, including
                anything typed through the virtual keyboard or triggered by the
                automated jiggler and its coding emulator. Do not use the
                application to defeat security controls, evade monitoring that you
                are not permitted to evade, or gain unauthorised access to any
                system. Where a mouse jiggler is prohibited by the policies of
                your employer or the owner of a machine, you are responsible for
                complying with those policies.
            </p>

            <h2>3. Hardware and Bluetooth compatibility</h2>
            <p>
                The application relies on the Bluetooth Human Interface Device
                profile. Whether a particular host accepts it depends on that
                host's Bluetooth stack and configuration, which is outside the
                developer's control. Some hosts require the pairing to be
                completed from the host side, and some do not accept a combined
                keyboard and mouse device at all. The application is provided
                as is, without any guarantee that it will pair with every device.
            </p>

            <h2>4. Intellectual property</h2>
            <p>
                The application, its name, its icon and its source code are
                licensed to you under the terms above. Unless stated otherwise,
                all content on this website, including the written copy and the
                brand assets, may be reproduced for editorial and informational
                purposes with attribution and a link back to this site. Please
                ask before using the name or the icon in a way that implies an
                official endorsement.
            </p>

            <h2>5. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
            <p>
                The application and this website are provided "as is", without
                warranty of any kind, express or implied, including but not
                limited to the warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
                particular purpose and non-infringement. The developer does not
                warrant that the application will be uninterrupted, error free or
                compatible with any particular device or host.
            </p>

            <h2>6. Limitation of liability</h2>
            <p>
                To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the developer
                shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special,
                consequential or punitive damages, or for any loss of data, loss
                of profits, loss of goodwill or business interruption, arising out
                of or in connection with the application or this website, whether
                in contract, tort or otherwise, even if the developer has been
                advised of the possibility of such damages.
            </p>

            <h2>7. Privacy</h2>
            <p>
                The application collects no personal data and requests no Android
                internet permission. The
                <a href={`${base}/privacy/`}>privacy policy</a> sets out the full
                details, including every permission the app asks for and why.
            </p>

            <h2>8. Changes to these terms</h2>
            <p>
                These terms may be updated as the application changes. The current
                version is always published on this page with its date. Continued
                use of the application after an update constitutes acceptance of
                the revised terms.
            </p>

            <h2>9. Contact</h2>
            <p>
                Questions about these terms can be sent to
                <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>

<style>
    .legal {
        padding-block: clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 2vw, 3rem) clamp(3rem, 2rem + 3vw, 4rem);
    }

    .legal__crumbs {
        display: flex;
        gap: 0.5rem;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        color: var(--ink-3);
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }

    .legal__crumbs a {
        color: var(--ink-2);
        text-decoration: none;
    }

    .legal__crumbs a:hover {
        color: var(--brand);
    }

    .legal__head {
        padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .legal__updated {
        margin-top: 0.5rem;
        font-size: 0.88rem;
        color: var(--ink-3);
    }

    .legal__body {
        max-width: 72ch;
    }
</style>
